
"smart_sources:2026-05-16 - At Kempthorne’s funeral, Dad and Pop Dirk remembered along with the public servant.md": {"path":"2026-05-16 - At Kempthorne’s funeral, Dad and Pop Dirk remembered along with the public servant.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"4yxgt","at":1785795032779},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783544299985,"size":8817,"at":1785795032967,"hash":"4yxgt"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,27],"##Dirk Kempthorne was more than his titles":[28,53],"##Dirk Kempthorne was more than his titles#{1}":[30,53],"##He was Dad and Pop Dirk":[54,86],"##He was Dad and Pop Dirk#{1}":[56,86]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Shannon Tyler","target":"Shannon Tyler","line":5},{"title":"Following a ceremony honoring former Idaho Gov. Dirk Kempthorne, current Gov. Brad Little gives Patricia Kempthorne a hug near the casket in the Idaho State Capitol rotunda, Friday, May 15, 2026.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/ahhst1/picture315772744/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_0515kempthorne01casketgov.JPG","line":24,"embedded":true},{"title":"Gov. Dirk Kempthorne, who has made a point of personally greeting Idaho troops in training and on active duty, visits the 1-183rd Aviation Battalion at Fort Hood on Friday. Of the 430 who will be deployed to Afghanistan in February, 250 are from Idaho.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/tv0819/picture313657354/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_dk2006deploymenttroops.JPG","line":38,"embedded":true},{"title":"Former Idaho Gov. Dirk Kempthorne, center, and former Idaho first lady Patricia Kempthorne, right, are recognized at the State of the State address, Jan. 12, 2026. At left are former Idaho first lady Vicki Risch and U.S. Sen. Jim Risch, R-Idaho, who served as Kempthorne’s lieutenant governor and his successor as governor.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/p5r2gw/picture314319834/alternates/FREE_1200/0112%2022%20state%20of%20state.jpg","line":50,"embedded":true},{"title":"Dirk Kempthorne, center, former Idaho governor, and wife Patricia Kempthorne, right, have seven grandchildren, who call him “Pop Dirk.”","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/br8s7p/picture313632347/alternates/FREE_1200/Kempthorne_Grandchildren.jpg","line":68,"embedded":true},{"title":"Idaho Gov. Dirk Kempthorne, right, prays with his wife Patricia, center, and daughter Heather, left, in his office before walking across the Statehouse to the House Chambers where he delivered his State of the State address to the 58th Idaho Legislature in January 2005. Kempthorne indicated in his speech that he would not seek a third term.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/qoc77y/picture313657356/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_dk2005prayer.JPG","line":80,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"At Kempthorne’s funeral, Dad and Pop Dirk remembered along with the public servant","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/northwest/idaho/article315783542.html#campaignName=boise_politics_newsletter","author":["[[Shannon Tyler]]"],"published":"2026-05-16","created":"2026-07-08","description":"“My dad had this incredible curiosity about people. He didn’t just meet you, he saw you. It didn’t matter who you were.”"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},